00:00:54.190 --> 00:01:02.719
Anyway, so I cannot that, um, particularly
our two D party system, or at least our Congress

00:01:02.719 --> 00:01:10.240
could better from actually being completely
nonpartisan and not actually be partied whatsoever.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:16.439
I can't help but think that if they were,
if somehow we could make Congress complete

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:20.889
like full of independent politicians that
it would actually function better.

00:01:20.889 --> 00:01:22.840
And I was wondering what you would think about
that.

00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:27.079
In a lot of ways it would, and there are local
elections that are done in this way where

00:01:27.079 --> 00:01:33.389
you might have an individual who personally
say considers themselves a Republican and

00:01:33.389 --> 00:01:38.109
votes for Republicans nationally, but you
can have like a mayoral election for example,

00:01:38.109 --> 00:01:41.920
where there are no parties, uh, declared by
the candidates.

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:44.759
And so in order to figure out who to vote
for it, you actually have to look and see

00:01:44.759 --> 00:01:50.209
what are people's policy platforms, what are
people's positions on policies.

00:01:50.209 --> 00:01:53.639
And it is very appealing to people like me.

00:01:53.639 --> 00:02:00.279
It sounds like to people like you because
we see the party label as more of a problem

00:02:00.279 --> 00:02:05.999
